{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FGC6jqQCZzNW5QHb4DsRwJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Book Stage B3 — Retrieval-Practice Architecture\n2\t\n3\tPer the skill's Part 10, 20-25% of checkpoint questions in chapters 3+ should test earlier material. Plan this explicitly at book level so later chapters know what to call back to.\n4\t\n5\t## The skill\n6\t\n7\t{{skill}}\n8\t\n9\t## Chapter lineup\n10\t\n11\t{{chapter_lineup}}\n12\t\n13\t## Your task\n14\t\n15\tProduce `retrieval-architecture.md`:\n16\t\n17\t```markdown\n18\t# Retrieval-Practice Architecture — {{book_exam_code}}\n19\t\n20\t## Target spacing\n21\t\n22\tPer skill Part 10:\n23\t\n24\t| Chapter | % questions from earlier chapters |\n25\t|---|---|\n26\t| 1–2 | 0% |\n27\t| 3 | 10% |\n28\t| 4 | 15% |\n29\t| 5+ | 20–25% |\n30\t\n31\t## Retrieval schedule\n32\t\n33\tFor each chapter 3+:\n34\t\n35\t| Chapter | Retrieval targets (earlier-chapter concepts) | Rationale |\n36\t|---|---|---|\n37\t| 3 | concept-X (ch 1), concept-Y (ch 2) | X is a prerequisite for ch 3's main topic |\n38\t| ... | | |\n39\t\n40\t## Cross-cutting themes\n41\t\n42\tConcepts that recur across many chapters and should receive repeated retrieval attention (e.g., \"declarative desired state\" in a Kubernetes book, \"CIA triad\" in a security book).\n43\t```\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46592f22-bd5b-4945-b7f7-384f0a58414e","uuid":"4dfa498e-13f0-4bd1-b934-fd2f6c921f06","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:12:19.906Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\pipeline\\prompts\\book\\B03_retrieval_architecture.md","content":"# Book Stage B3 — Retrieval-Practice Architecture\n\nPer the skill's Part 10, 20-25% of checkpoint questions in chapters 3+ should test earlier material. Plan this explicitly at book level so later chapters know what to call back to.\n\n## The skill\n\n{{skill}}\n\n## Chapter lineup\n\n{{chapter_lineup}}\n\n## Your task\n\nProduce `retrieval-architecture.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Retrieval-Practice Architecture — {{book_exam_code}}\n\n## Target spacing\n\nPer skill Part 10:\n\n| Chapter | % questions from earlier chapters |\n|---|---|\n| 1–2 | 0% |\n| 3 | 10% |\n| 4 | 15% |\n| 5+ | 20–25% |\n\n## Retrieval schedule\n\nFor each chapter 3+:\n\n| Chapter | Retrieval targets (earlier-chapter concepts) | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3 | concept-X (ch 1), concept-Y (ch 2) | X is a prerequisite for ch 3's main topic |\n| ... | | |\n\n## Cross-cutting themes\n\nConcepts that recur across many chapters and should receive repeated retrieval attention (e.g., \"declarative desired state\" in a Kubernetes book, \"CIA triad\" in a security book).\n```\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
